    "body": "Adds a macOS Stow package `devonthink-open`.\n\n- `dt-open` looks each PDF up in every open DEVONthink database (`lookup records with path`, as in the DT forum threads) and opens the `x-devonthink-item://` link; PDFs that are not indexed go to a fallback viewer (Preview, configurable) and never to DEVONthink.\n- `dt-open-install` builds `DT Open PDF.app` (an applet that calls `dt-open`), registers it for `com.adobe.pdf` and makes it the default PDF viewer, so Finder double-click and Alfred's file picker both use it. `--uninstall` restores the previous default.\n- Not run on a Mac. Tested here: bash syntax and `dt-open`'s decisions against stand-ins for `osascript`/`open`. Untested: the AppleScript lookup, `osacompile`/`PlistBuddy`/`codesign`, and LaunchServices registration.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNiBSPryU16ZirHGRiaX)_",
